=09=09All About Arteries =20
=09=09
=09=09An artery is a blood vessel that carries blood away from the heart. M=
ost=20
arteries carry bright red, oxygen-rich blood to all parts of your body. The=
re=20
are two exceptions to this. The first is the pulmonary artery, which carrie=
s=20
deoxygenated (oxygen-poor) blood from the heart to the lungs where the bloo=
d=20
is able to pick up oxygen. The second is the umbilical artery, which carrie=
s=20
deoxygenated blood from the fetus back toward the mother's heart.
