=09=09
=09=09Carpal tunnel syndrome is a term for an overuse injury of the nerve t=
hat runs=20
through the "carpal tunnel," a sheath in the wrist area. This syndrome=20
usually occurs when the wrist is overused, such as with repetitive work and=
=20
while typing. Pain, numbness, tingling, and weakness of the wrist and hand=
=20
can all be symptoms of this condition. If you have any of these symptoms, s=
ee=20
your physician.
